- [novelty_killer, systems_reviewer] Mechanism collision verified ≥2 independent sources: SpecDec++ (arXiv:2405.19715) and Dynamic-Speculation-Lookahead/DISCO (arXiv:2405.04304) both adapt draft length from a runtime signal at PER-STEP granularity — strictly finer than the proposed coarse 3-phase session policy. SGLang ships adaptive speculative decoding in production. The proposed method is a degenerate (coarser) special case of published and deployed methods.
- [all 5 reviewers] The ONLY potential differentiator — beating best-tuned-fixed on agentic session-phase drift — does not hold. Packet's own L0 sweep (3,024 configs): tuned-fixed captures 92.7% median of adaptive gain; adaptive loses −2.22% mean net tok/s at the realistic operating point (p_err>0, s>0). All 3 pre-registered negative triggers fired.
