RATIONALE:
Aggregation note: The 3 RED and 2 GREEN votes are not in disagreement. The two GREEN votes (evaluation_prosecutor, theory_skeptic) endorse the QUALITY of the negative result — the methodology is sound, pre-registered, uses the correct baseline, and the Jensen-floor mechanism is theoretically well-grounded. The three RED votes (novelty_killer, systems_reviewer, product_realist) independently confirm that no contribution survives: the mechanism is published in ≥4 works and shipped in SGLang, the only differentiator failed, and no production use case exists. All five reviewers agree the claim is dead; they differ only on whether to praise the methodology (GREEN) or flag the absence of surviving contribution (RED). Evidence resolves this unambiguously toward KILL.

The claim had two legs: (A) drift exists, (B) adaptive beats best-tuned-fixed. Leg (A) is confirmed but is not novel — SpecDec++ (arXiv:2405.19715) and DISCO (arXiv:2405.04304) already exploit acceptance variation at finer granularity than session-phase. Leg (B) is falsified by the packet's own pre-registered L0 (tuned-fixed captures ~93% median; adaptive −2.2% net with overhead). The Jensen-floor mechanism (broad overlapping plateaus of the (E[accepted]+1)/(k·r+1) curve) is the same geometry that killed EXP-0006 and EXP-0011, making this the third independent confirmation of a structural negative on the adaptive-knob-vs-tuned-baseline axis.

An L1 GPU pass is not warranted: the L0 analytic ceiling (≤~9% ideal, negative with overhead) bounds the real-hardware result from above, and the mechanism explanation (concave plateau overlap) is independent of hardware substrate. The question is closed.

The anti-hallucination rule was honored: novelty_killer cited 4 works with retrievable arXiv URLs, collision verified in ≥2 independent sources (SpecDec++, DISCO). Systems_reviewer independently found SGLang's shipping implementation. No reviewer used "novel/promising/significant" without a cited metric or named prior work.

VERDICT: KILL. CLAIM-0026 is terminal. This is a clean honest negative — the research pipeline worked correctly. The pre-registration, the best-tuned-fixed baseline discipline (learned from EXP-0006), and the honest reporting are exemplary. The claim is dead; the methodology is sound; the Jensen-floor pattern on this axis is now robustly established across three independent experiments.
